{meta title='Every PAD type'/}
<section class="hero">
  <h1>Every PAD type</h1>
  <p class="lead">A tag has a type, the prefix before the colon: <code>&#123;pad:if&#125;</code> is a
  built-in tag, <code>&#123;chart:pie&#125;</code> a chart type, <code>&#123;field:name&#125;</code>
  a field of the row, <code>&#123;sequence:fibonacci&#125;</code> a sequence. Written without its
  prefix a name is the first type that has it. A page for each type: what it reaches, how it is
  written, where it stands in the order a bare name is tried in, the tags it has and live examples.</p>
  <ul class="stats">
    <li><b>{$typesCount}</b> types</li>
    <li><b>{$memberCount}</b> tags they reach by name</li>
    <li><b>{$exampleCount}</b> examples</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<div class="cards">
  {indexes}
  <a class="card" href="?{$page}">
    <h2>{$label}</h2>
    <p>{$text}</p>
  </a>
  {/indexes}
</div>

<h2>The groups</h2>
<div class="cards">
  {groups}
  <section class="card">
    <h3><a href="?groups#{$key}">{$label}</a> <span class="count">{$count}</span></h3>
    <p>{$tagline}</p>
    <div class="tagcloud">{types}<a href="?{$link}" title="{$about}">{$key}</a>{/types}</div>
  </section>
  {/groups}
</div>
